{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And you shall command.</b> Everything said until now as וְעָשִׂיתָ is understood to mean that it would be made through another. But here, that he should command — this means he should command the craftsmen to make it. Therefore, regarding these three commandments that He commanded, it says וְאַתָּה, to inform him that the making is by himself: that he should command Israel concerning the preparation of the oil, and that he should bring Aaron and his sons to him (Exodus 28:1), and that he should speak to all who are wise of heart (Exodus 28:3)." "<b>And they shall take to you.</b> When needed — and this will be when the oil for the lamp that they now donated in the dedication of the Tabernacle runs out, so that they should not suppose that the commandment of kindling the Menorah was merely a one-time command limited to that oil which they donated."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:27.144593224Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}